        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Stalinism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1924 CE – 1953 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Joseph Stalin</a>, who developed socialism in one country; Lazar Kaganovich, who reportedly proposed replacing “Long Live Leninism” with “Long Live Stalinism”; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikolai-bukharin">Nikolai Bukharin</a>, whose Right Opposition was defeated; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-trotsky">Leon Trotsky</a>, its foremost critic, who promoted permanent revolution; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikita-khrushchev">Nikita Khrushchev</a>, who denounced it in 1956; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha">Enver Hoxha</a>, whose Hoxhaism kept a version of it in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albania">Albania</a></span></div>
